course: dictionary
lesson: 8446
title: Sag: sinking, drooping and dips
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sag means to sink or hang down, often because something is heavy, old or tired. You can see the clue in the sentence. «The shelf sagged under the heavy books.» Heavy books make the shelf bend down, so sagged means sank down in the middle.
explain: Sag can also mean to become weaker or lower, especially for feelings or numbers. «Her shoulders sagged when she heard the news.» Shoulders cannot be heavy here, so the clue is the news. She felt sad or tired, and her shoulders drooped.
explain: Sag can be a noun too, meaning a dip or a place that has sunk down. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The tent had a sag in the middle.» Does "a dip in the middle" still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Sag means to sink or hang down, often because of weight, age or tiredness.
fact: «Sagged» is the past tense of sag, and «sagging» is the -ing form.
fact: «A long bridge with no support sags in the middle.» Engineers add triangles, arches or thicker layers to make it stiffer.
fact: «A camel's hump stores fat, not water, and the hump sags as the fat is used up.»
fact: Sag can also mean to become weaker or lower, as in «my spirits sagged» or «sales sagged».
exercise: «The shelf sagged under the heavy books.» What does sagged mean? | Was painted blue | *Sank down in the middle under weight | Shone brightly | Jumped high into the air
exercise: «Her shoulders sagged when she heard the news.» What does sagged suggest? | She was very excited | *She felt sad or tired and gave up | She was cold and wet | She stood up tall
exercise: Engineers say «a long bridge sags in the middle unless you add triangles or an arch.» What helps stop a bridge sagging? | Taking away its arch | Making it longer with no support | Painting it red | *Adding triangles or an arch
test: Which word means became weaker or lower? | Shone | Stood | *Sagged | Bounced
test: «The sagging roof needs fixing before winter.» What does sagging mean here? | *Sinking down under weight or age | Shining in the sun | Bouncing back up | Singing loudly
exam: What does a camel's hump store, so that it sags as the fat is used up? | Air | Sand | Water | *Fat
